# {{ project_slug }}

A self-contained Python package with a two-task Databricks job: build the wheel from workspace source and upload it to a Unity Catalog Volume, then install and verify it.

## Prerequisites

- [Databricks CLI](https://docs.databricks.com/dev-tools/cli/install.html) v0.230+, authenticated (`databricks auth login`)
- Unity Catalog enabled
- Permission to create catalogs in the metastore — the bundle creates catalog `{{ cfg.catalog }}` on deploy

## What's here

```
pyproject.toml                        # Package metadata (hatchling build backend)
src/custom_python_wheel/
├── __init__.py                       # Public API exports
└── functions.py                      # greet() and add() — replace with your own
notebooks/
├── build_and_upload.py               # Builds wheel, creates schema+volume, uploads
└── verify_imports.py                 # Installs wheel, asserts functions work
resources/jobs/wheel_job.yml          # Two-task job: build → verify
```

## Deploy

```bash
databricks bundle validate --target dev
databricks bundle deploy --target dev
databricks bundle run {{ project_slug | replace("-", "_") }}_wheel --target dev
```

## Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `catalog` | `{{ cfg.catalog }}` | Catalog for the wheel volume |
| `schema` | `{{ cfg.schema }}` | Schema for the wheel volume |

## Extending the package

Add new modules under `src/custom_python_wheel/` and export them from `__init__.py`. Add assertions to `notebooks/verify_imports.py` for each new function. Bump `version` in `pyproject.toml` when you release a new build — the job always picks up the latest wheel matching `custom_python_wheel-*.whl` in the volume, so no separate publish step is needed during development.

## Troubleshooting

- **"Catalog does not exist"** — create `{{ cfg.catalog }}` (or your override) before deploying.
- **`verify_imports` fails to find the wheel** — confirm `build_and_upload` ran successfully first; the job is defined with a task dependency, but re-running `verify_imports` alone will fail if no wheel has been uploaded yet.
